<Article
  title="Free food, free water, named by the label"
  description="Beautiful second-life rooms that bring people back to nature, one room at a time."
  kicker="The hope"
  date="2026-09-30"
>
  <p>The farm units can already be asked for. H20, the water unit, comes later and still needs further research. The network around either of them does not exist yet. This note is that hope, written so it cannot be mistaken for a signup.</p>
  <RevealHeading as="h2">The exchange</RevealHeading>
  <p>A person takes food, or a jug of water, and does not pay. An advertiser’s name is on that food or that jug. The role of Aura Homes, if the network is built, is the advertising placement and the rooms, not a toll on the person who is thirsty or hungry.</p>
  <p>The same room can skip the network. An owner who buys a farm wall can keep the harvest. A bottling line, once H20 is past research, could be used the same way. The network is a choice we want to offer later. The farm unit is the choice available to ask about now.</p>
  <RevealHeading as="h2">What the network means here</RevealHeading>
  <p>It means a repeated way to place rooms, fill jugs, harvest a wall, and carry an advertiser’s label under one set of rules. It does not mean a territory for sale, a fee schedule, or a brand you can license this month. There is no advertiser marketplace on this site.</p>
  <RevealHeading as="h2">Why say it now</RevealHeading>
  <p>The rooms, the <a href="/farms">farm walls</a>, and the <a href="/water">water unit</a> are easier to understand if the longer aim is visible. People who only want a room should still be able to find the room, and stop there. People who want to grow can ask for a farm unit and ignore the network. People who want water from the air can read the H20 page and wait for the research. People who want to help build the free distribution can enquire with that aim named.</p>
  <p>Until an advertiser has actually paid, and a jug has actually been given away, the honest sentence is the one above: this is what we hope to accomplish.</p>
</Article>
